// ── Beloved identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The ONE place for the app's final identifiers. Everything else derives from them:
//
//   App                    $(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX)
//   Shield Configuration   $(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX).ShieldConfiguration
//   Shield Action          $(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX).ShieldAction
//   Activity Monitor       $(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX).ActivityMonitor
//   UI tests               $(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX).UITests
//   App Group              group.$(PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX)
//
// Neither value is secret (both are visible in every signed build), so commit them once
// chosen. Use a reverse-DNS prefix you own; never another developer's identifier.
// Until set, unsigned/simulator compiles still work, and the "Validate
// release readiness" build phase stops any archive (App Store / TestFlight). See
// docs/12-signing-setup.md.
//
// Per-developer overrides (e.g. a personal team for device testing) can go in the
// git-ignored Config/Secrets.xcconfig, which is included after this file.

// Placeholder (not a real identifier). Replace with a reverse-DNS prefix you own,
// e.g. com.<your-domain>.beloved — never a guess.
PL_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX = unconfigured.beloved
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
